# Exceptions to the reviewable change size limit in docs/QUALITY.md.
#
#   path <glob>    # why this content is not reviewable
#   branch <name>  # why this change cannot be split
#
# `*` stops at a slash, `**` crosses them. The rationale is required: a reason nothing checks for
# is a reason that stops being written. Prefer splitting the branch to allowlisting it -- a `path`
# entry says the content is not read line by line, and a `branch` entry says a reviewer will read
# more in one pass than the limit assumes.
#
# Repository-layout exclusions -- lockfiles, generated DB artifacts, the generated skill mirror --
# are in scripts/just/check-pr-size.cjs instead. They are properties of the tree, not exceptions
# anyone reviewed.

path test/fixtures/** # recorded upstream responses and sample documents, verified by replay rather than by reading
branch claude/task-t-0026-elevated-access-ttb5y8 # T-0026 milestone 4 is one safety rule in three places -- the predicate that says who is waiting on a decision, the controls that take it, and the guard at the mutation that re-checks the evidence before the write. Splitting it ships a half where a write path exists without the guard, which is the exact defect this branch's review found three times. 857 of the 1574 lines are tests
